<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n101726" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφός</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφή,
		σφόν</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>their, their
				own, belonging to them</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				1.534
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Sapph.
				10
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Pi.
				<u>P.</u>
				5.102
			</span></i>, etc. (never in 
				Att.
			). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> in post-<i><span class="en">
				Hom.
			</span></i> Poets also, <i>his</i> or <i>her, his own</i> or <i>her
				own</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Th.</u>
				398
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Alcm.
				56
			</span></i>A, <i><span class="en">
				Thgn.
				712
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Call.
				<u>Aet.Oxy.</u>
				2080.75
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Orph.
				<u>L.</u>
				168
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐμός</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				<u>CR</u>
				11.136
			</span></i> (Phrygia, metr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφωΐτερος</span>
			, <i>your</i> (in addressing a pair), v.l. in
			<i><span class="en">
				Il.
				11.142
			</span></i>. (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφός</span> is to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σφε</span><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">,
			σφέτερος</span> as <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Ἡμός
				</span>(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμός</span>) to <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁμέ, ἡμέτερος</span>.)</div>
